REST APIS:

what are rest apis?:
- Representational state transfer
- uses HTTP:
- to access the resources of a server , client will do a HTTP request via a "web browser" by sending 
    - request header
    - request payload
- gets the response back in response body, status code etc
- there are different methods to do a REST HTTP request
    - `GET,POST,PUT,PATCH,DELETE`
    - idempotent methods are the methods no matter how many times you call them, they have same effect on the resources 
        - ex: GET,PUT,PATCH,DELETE
        - ! sometimes patch is not idempotent as well, because it alters only a part of the resource instead of whole resource
    - non idempotent methods are the methods each time you call them the resource will also be get affected
        - ex: POST -! be carefull while using this.
        - PATCH is idempotent if it sets a specific value or performs an operation that does not depend on the current state of the resource.
        - PATCH is non-idempotent if it modifies the resource in a way that depends on its current state (e.g., incrementing a value, appending to a list, etc.).

